  "🤝 自動接手（第 {n}/{max} 次）：{action}{guidance}": "🤝 Auto-resume ({n}/{max}): {action}{guidance}",
  "——{guidance}": " — {guidance}",
  "✅ 自動循環已達步數上限，已自動停止。要接著討論或調整，直接在這張交辦回覆即可；要再自動接續就重開開關。": "✅ Autopilot reached its step limit and stopped. To keep discussing or adjust, just reply on this assignment; switch it back on to auto-continue.",
  "✅ 自動循環已達時間上限，已自動停止。要接著討論或調整，直接在這張交辦回覆即可；要再自動接續就重開開關。": "✅ Autopilot reached its time limit and stopped. To keep discussing or adjust, just reply on this assignment; switch it back on to auto-continue.",
  "🅿️ 自動循環正常結束{reason}。要接著討論或調整，直接在這張交辦回覆即可（有專屬團隊會由同一隊接手）；要再自動接續就重開開關。": "🅿️ Autopilot finished normally{reason}. To keep discussing or adjust, just reply on this assignment (a dedicated team resumes with the same crew); switch it back on to auto-continue.",
  "工作階段已中止；請重新下指令": "Session was interrupted; please send the command again",
  "探索失敗": "Discovery failed",
  "⛔ 探索失敗：{error}": "⛔ Discovery failed: {error}",
  "\n\n【驗證步驟的取捨（預設不加 review）】Review 是例外，不是預設，不要為了看起來嚴謹而加。撰寫文件／內容／說明、或建立檔案與資料這類產出，即使跨多個檔案、需依序完成、或要彼此一致，預設都不加獨立 review——由執行者在自己的步驟裡自我檢查即可，一致性也由後續 execute 步驟自己顧。只有「程式邏輯、設定、計算，或其正確性一旦錯了會造成實際故障」的產出，才值得在其 execute 後緊接一個 review（且由不同 NPC 負責）。低風險、機械式、或執行者當場就能自我驗證的步驟一律不加 review：execute 步驟本身已要求自我驗證，多排一個 review 只會拖慢。永遠優先用最少步驟達成目標。": "\n\n[When to add a verification step — default to NONE] A review is the exception, not the default; do not add one just to look rigorous. Authoring documents/content/explanations, or creating files and data, does NOT get a separate review by default — even across multiple files, sequential steps, or when they must stay consistent; the executor self-checks within its own step, and consistency is handled by the later execute steps themselves. Add a review after an execute step ONLY for program logic, configuration, or calculations whose incorrectness would cause a real failure (and assign it to a different NPC). Low-risk, mechanical, or self-verifiable steps never get a review: the execute step already requires self-verification, and an extra review only slows things down. Always prefer the fewest steps that achieve the goal.",
  "：{reason}": ": {reason}",
